An AI agent that can act autonomously also creates a new privacy problem: its identity, messages, payments and working data can become separate points of exposure.

That makes Beldex’s current AI direction more interesting as a stack than as a single feature.

@BeldexCoin is exploring privacy-preserving agent identities through BNS, encrypted AI-powered communication through BChat, confidential payments, secure AI execution and FHE-based confidential computation. The important detail is their relationship: an agent may need privacy across several stages of the same operation, not only while a model is processing data.

There is also a clear boundary between what exists and what is still being developed. BNS and BChat already belong to the Beldex ecosystem; FHE and several agent-focused capabilities remain areas of research and development.

For autonomous software, protecting one action while exposing the surrounding workflow would leave a large privacy gap. Beldex’s approach is increasingly aimed at that workflow as a whole.
